      "commit": "f5f6acfb1cd8afada18d556a40a200e7072b4d33",
      "disposition": "partially-adapted-net-state",
      "rationale": "Complete eight-file original fscrypt inline-encryption patch examined. Native configuration/build integration, content-only selection, mode mapping, key setup/eviction and bio/DUN interfaces now provide the feature. Preserve native all-device capability checks, variable DUN widths including direct-key support, per-data-unit geometry and RCU keyed-list lifetime; do not restore raw-key arrays, eight-byte DUN BUG_ON, old callback mount option or early crypt-info dereference. Current inline zeroout uses the separately reviewed asynchronous implementation; Android metadata skip-state extensions remain in the shared helpers. Key bytes are wiped and evicted through native current APIs.",
